This project is a Kotlin port of
"amazon-sqs-java-extended-client-lib"
(https://github.com/awslabs/amazon-sqs-java-extended-client-lib):

    Copyright 2010-2020 Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

This is a derivative work under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The message-offload
control flow, receipt-handle pointer embedding, message-attribute validation, and S3 key
prefix rules in src/main/kotlin/com/christophsens/sqsoverflow/SqsExtendedClient.kt,
SqsExtendedClientConfig.kt, and SqsExtendedClientConstants.kt are ported from the
corresponding logic in the original's AmazonSQSExtendedClient, AmazonSQSExtendedClientBase,
AmazonSQSExtendedClientUtil, SQSExtendedClientConstants, and ExtendedClientConfiguration,
translated from Java to Kotlin. See the copyright header in each of those files for the
original attribution.

Changes made in this port:

  * The original's separate AmazonSQSExtendedClient (SqsClient) and
    AmazonSQSExtendedAsyncClient (SqsAsyncClient) are consolidated into a single
    SqsExtendedClient, since aws-sdk-kotlin's SqsClient is already suspend-based.
  * The ~1150-line pass-through base class (AmazonSQSExtendedClientBase) is replaced by
    Kotlin interface delegation (`SqsClient by sqsClient`).
  * payloadoffloading-common (PayloadStore/S3BackedPayloadStore/S3Dao/Util/PayloadS3Pointer)
    is replaced by s3overflow (https://github.com/christoph-sens/s3overflow), itself a
    from-scratch Kotlin reimplementation of payload-offloading-java-common-lib-for-aws.
  * ExtendedClientConfiguration's ObjectCannedACL/ServerSideEncryptionStrategy
    configuration, the legacy SQSLargePayloadSize attribute name toggle, and the
    deprecated pre-PayloadStorageConfiguration aliases are dropped. Core behavior —
    threshold-based offloading, alwaysThroughS3, cleanupS3Payload, s3KeyPrefix,
    ignorePayloadNotFound — is preserved.

The receipt-handle and pointer JSON formats produced by this port are therefore not
byte-identical to the original's, except for the RESERVED_ATTRIBUTE_NAME value
("ExtendedPayloadSize"), which is kept unchanged for interop with the original's documented
SNSExtendedClient-shared attribute name.

